\]  
Thus, the complex `[Pt(NH3)₄Cl₂]Cl₂` dissociates into `[Pt(NH₃)₄Cl₂]²⁺` and 2 `Cl⁻` ions.  

The chloride ions are derived from the two `Cl⁻` ions in the complex formula.  

Thus, the number of chloride ions produced is 2.  

