2. Postiyllic isomerism: Different positions of the hydroxyl group (-OH) on the carbon chain.
3. Posnd-chain or branched chain isomerism: Presence of a methyl group or other alkyl groups at different positions on the carbon chain.
3. Stereoisomerism: Different spatial arrangement of atoms in space.

This includes:
a. E/Z isomerism (cis/trans)
b. Meso isomers
c. Diastereomers

For example, the isomers of C4H10O are:
- 1-butanol (primary alcohol)
- 2-butanol (secondary alcohol)
- 3-butanol (secondary alcohol)
- 2-methyl-2-propanol (tertiary alcohol)
