1. Temperature-responsive polymers: These polymers undergo changes in their properties (e.g., solubility, viscosity, degradation) upon temperature changes. Examples include block polymers like poly(N-isopropylacrylamide) (PNIPAM) and thermo-responsive block copolymers. Examples include block polymers like poly(N-isopropylacrylate) (PNIPA). These polymers have a lower critical temperature (LCST) at which they transition from a swollen, swollen to a collapsed state.

