   - Amplitude: \( |2| = 2 \)
   - Period: \( \frac{2\pi}{3} \)

The period of \( f(x) \) is the least common multiple (LCM) of the periods of the two functions:
- Amplitude of \( f(x) \) is the sum of the amplitudes: \( 3 + 2 = 5 \).
