   \]

2. **Calculate the kinetic energy**:
   \[
   \text{K.E.} = \frac{1}{2} m v^2
   \]
   Substituting the values:
   \[
   \text{K.E.} = \frac{1}{2} \times 400 \text{ kg} \times (800 \text{ m/s})^2 = 200 \times 640000 = 12800000 \text{ J} = 128 \text{ J}
