- \( \mu_0 \) is the permeability of free space (\( 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T} \cdot \text{m} \cdot \text{m} \cdot \text{s} \)).
- \( r \) is the radius of the coil.
- \( I \) is the current through the coil.

For a coil with \( N \) turns, the formula becomes:

\[
B = \frac{\mu_0 N}{2\pi r} \cdot I
\]

Substituting the given values:
- \( N = 100 \) turns
- \( I = 1 \, \text{A} \)
- \( r = 0.2 \, \text{m} \)
- \( \mu_0 = 4\pi \times 10^{-7} \, \text{T} \cdot \text{m} \cdot \text{m} \cdot \text{s} \)

\[
