","To compute the natural frequencies and mode shapes of the bllet dish, we analyze the system as a system of three masses connected by springs. The stiffness constants are:  
- \( k_t \) is the torsional stiffness of each blade.  
- \( K_c \) is the coupling stiffness between blades.  

The stiffness matrix \( K \) is given by:  
\[
K = \begin{pmatrix} k_t + K_c & -K_c & 0 \\
-K_c & k_t + K_c & -K_c \\
0 & -K_c & k_t + K_c
\end{pmatrix}
\]  
Substituting the given values:  
\[
K = \begin{pmatrix} 430,000 + 45,430 & -45,430 & 0 \\
-45,430 & 430,000 + 44,330 & -45,430 \\
0 & -45,330 & 430,000 + 45,330
\end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 475,430 & -45,430 & 0 \\
-45,430 & 474,330 & -45,430 \\
0 & -45,330 & 475,330
\end{pmatrix}
\]  
The mass matrix \( M \) is a diagonal matrix with mass \( m_t \) for each blade:  
\[
M = \begin{pmatrix} m_t & 0 & 0 \\
0 & m_t & 0 \\
0 & 0 & m_t
\end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0.0114 & 0 & 0 \\
0 & 0.0114 & 0 \\
0 & 0 & 0.0114
endpmatrix
\]  
The characteristic equation is:  
\[
\begin{vmatrix} K - \lambda M \end{pmatrix} = 0
\]  
