A toroidal coil 1 with $N_1$ turns and a toroidal coil 2 with $N_2$ turns are arranged such that coil 2 encircles the magnetic field formed inside coil 1. The coils have cross-sectional areas $A$ and the circumference of the axial circles of the toroids is $\ell$. If an alternating current $I_1(t)$ flows in coil 1, and the r.m.s. voltage of the source is $V_0$, what is the reading on the voltmeter connected to coil 2?<end_of_turn>
